@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant — contrast XOR / OR / AND / event-based gateways.
'   usecase:      One fragment showing each gateway type with when-to-use notes.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       business-process
' ============================================================================
title Example BPMN Process - Gateway Types (Variant)

' Gateway cheat-sheet. PlantUML has no native BPMN; all gateways are
' rendered as diamond `usecase` shapes and labelled by their semantics.

' --- Inputs shared --------------------------------------------------------
usecase " " as Start
usecase " " as End

' --- Exclusive (XOR) — data-based ----------------------------------------
usecase "XOR\n(data)" as X1
usecase "XOR\nA" as Xa
usecase "XOR\nB" as Xb

' --- Inclusive (OR) ------------------------------------------------------
usecase "OR\n(inclusive)" as O1
usecase "OR\nA" as Oa
usecase "OR\nB" as Ob
usecase "OR\nMerge" as Om

' --- Parallel (AND) ------------------------------------------------------
usecase "AND\n(parallel)" as A1
usecase "AND\nA" as Aa
usecase "AND\nB" as Ab
usecase "AND\nMerge" as Am

' --- Event-based ---------------------------------------------------------
usecase "Event-based" as E1
usecase "Msg A" as Ea
usecase "Timer B" as Eb

Start --> X1
X1 --> Xa : if cond1
X1 --> Xb : if cond2

Start --> O1
O1 --> Oa : cond1
O1 --> Ob : cond2
Oa --> Om
Ob --> Om

Start --> A1
A1 --> Aa
A1 --> Ab
Aa --> Am
Ab --> Am

Start --> E1
E1 --> Ea : message arrives
E1 --> Eb : 1h timeout

Ea --> End
Eb --> End
Xa --> End
Xb --> End
Om --> End
Am --> End

note top of X1
  <b>Exclusive (XOR)</b>
  Exactly ONE path, chosen by
  data condition. No concurrency.
  Use: "if/else" branching.
end note

note top of O1
  <b>Inclusive (OR)</b>
  ONE or MORE paths, each evaluated
  independently. Merge waits for
  the active subset only.
  Use: optional add-ons that may stack.
end note

note top of A1
  <b>Parallel (AND)</b>
  ALL paths taken, no conditions.
  Merge waits for ALL.
  Use: independent concurrent work.
end note

note top of E1
  <b>Event-based</b>
  Branch on which EVENT fires first
  (message, timer, signal). The
  winner cancels the others.
  Use: race between external triggers.
end note

@enduml
